{"input_text": "Question: How can I calculate $$\int_{|z-i|=1}\frac{1}{z+i}\;dz$$ 
 It seems like the non-continuous point is: $z=-i$, and it is not inside the contour, would that mean that the integral is simply zero? 
 Thanks 

Answer: Cauchy Integral formula gives us
\begin{align}
f(a) = \oint_\gamma \dfrac{f(z)}{z-a} \,dz
\end{align} 
 Let $f(z) = 1 \; \forall z \in \mathbb{C}$, so, you are evaluating $f(-i)$, which by our definition is 1. 
